      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The city incorporated on February 28, 1949 after a cooperative brought electricity and tap water to residents.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonney_Lake%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bonney Lake sits along the historic Naches Trail, a well‑used immigrant and military route in the late 1800s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        11,
        13
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonney_Lake%2C_Washington",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Greater Bonney Lake Historical Society, formed in 2001, runs a small museum in the former city hall near Allan Yorke Park.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonney_Lake%2C_Washington",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The first wagon train on the unfinished “Immigrant Road” crossed the Cascades that fall, bringing settlers who founded nearby communities.",
